.TH "KOSH\-SWITCHING" "5" "October 28, 2026" "kosh" "Koshka Manual"
.SH NAME
kosh\-switching \- migrate an interactive shell environment and login
shell from Bash to Koshka
.PP
Prerequisites \- An installed \f[CR]kosh\f[R] binary, an active Bash
session, and a familiarity with kosh(1) invocation and kosh(5)
configuration.
.PP
Koshka is a command shell that controls execution behavior and startup
file loading through operational modes called moods.
The default \f[CR]kosh\f[R] mood checks shell code prior to execution
and rejects scripts containing errors.
The \f[CR]bash\f[R] mood provides Bash compatibility for startup
configurations and legacy scripts.
Try Koshka in a new terminal before changing the login shell, and keep
the current Bash session open in a separate terminal window while
testing startup files to prevent terminal lockout.
.SH CORE PRIMITIVES
.PP
.TS
